mized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/569408229","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9509#issuecomment-569408229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9509","id":569408229,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2OTQwODIyOQ==","user":{"login":"mattpap","id":27475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap","html_url":"https://github.com/mattpap","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattpap/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-12-28T11:21:23Z","updated_at":"2019-12-28T11:21:23Z","body":">  I'm not actually seeing what JS tests fail\r\n\r\nTest failures are currently showed only inline. We already discussed this, though there may not be an issue for this, and I'm going to improve reporting as time permits. If you don't see any errors inline and tests fail, then report a new issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/569408229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/569766682","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9509#issuecomment-569766682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9509","id":569766682,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2OTc2NjY4Mg==","user":{"login":"bryevdv","id":1078448,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg0NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1078448?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv","html_url":"https://github.com/bryevdv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-12-30T19:07:56Z","updated_at":"2019-12-30T19:07:56Z","body":"@mattpap @philippjfr this is still WIP but I would like some feedback. First, things to do:\r\n\r\n* expose further features of flatpickr\r\n* add more selenium tests\r\n\r\nBoth of those will be fairly easy/straightforward. I'd like some input on the properties changes. The current code around serializing dates and datetimes is a mess, so the current changes are also a mess, and that is what I would like input on.\r\n\r\nI think ideally what should happen is for scalar `datetime.date` values to render as ISO datestrings. These would be for individual `Date` properties, e.g. the value of the picker. But for everything else (i.e. `date` objects in arrays/series/columns) to transform as timestamps. Does this seem reasonable? \r\n\r\nCurrently this is not quite true -- series/arrays transform as timestamps but plain lists of dates become iso strings:\r\n```\r\nIn [6]: serialize_json(df.Date[:5])\r\nOut[6]: '[1356998400000.0,1357084800000.0,1357171200000.0,1357257600000.0,1357344000000.0]'\r\n\r\nIn [7]: serialize_json(list(df.Date[:5]))\r\nOut[7]: '[\"2013-01-01\",\"2013-01-02\",\"2013-01-03\",\"2013-01-04\",\"2013-01-05\"]'\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think the list case can be made consistent, though. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/569766682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/573477374","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9509#issuecomment-573477374","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9509","id":573477374,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MzQ3NzM3NA==","user":{"login":"bryevdv","id":1078448,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg0NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1078448?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv","html_url":"https://github.com/bryevdv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-13T00:44:58Z","updated_at":"2020-01-13T00:44:58Z","body":"> I think the list case can be made consistent, though.\r\n\r\nWell, I was wrong about this, but I think we just document it and live with it. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/573477374/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/573478916","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9509#issuecomment-573478916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9509","id":573478916,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MzQ3ODkxNg==","user":{"login":"bryevdv","id":1078448,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg0NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1078448?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv","html_url":"https://github.com/bryevdv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-13T01:00:19Z","updated_at":"2020-01-13T01:00:19Z","body":"@philippjfr can you test this with HV/Panel when you get a chance?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/573478916/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/573481730","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9509#issuecomment-573481730","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9509","id":573481730,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MzQ4MTczMA==","user":{"login":"bryevdv","id":1078448,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg0NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1078448?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv","html_url":"https://github.com/bryevdv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-13T01:27:16Z","updated_at":"2020-01-13T01:52:22Z","body":"@mattpap  @philippjfr  OK I think everything except plumbing to hook up whatever set of flatpickr features we want, is done. I hope to have this PR done done by tomorrow night. \r\n\r\n I think the Date/Datetime property situation is generally better. To summarize:\r\n\r\n* `Date` accepts `dt.date` values and ISO date strings (\"2020-01-11\") and, importantly, serializes as ISO datestring. This solves the nonsense with datepicker and time zones. \r\n\r\n* `Datetime` accepts:\r\n  - python, pandas, numpy datetime objects (including dt.time)\r\n  - dt.date and date strings\r\n  - ms since epoch timestamps\r\n  \r\n  and still serlializes as ms since epoch\r\n\r\nOne weird but anavoidable corner case: lists of `dt.date` get serialized as ISO strings, arrays and series `dt.date` get serialized as datetime/timestamp\r\n\r\nWeird stuff I noticed but did not touch: timedeltas and pandas Period values are serialized as datetimes. I think this is not the right thing to do, in general. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/573481730/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/574012025","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9509#issuecomment-574012025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9509","id":574012025,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NDAxMjAyNQ==","user":{"login":"bryevdv","id":1078448,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg0NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1078448?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv","html_url":"https://github.com/bryevdv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryevdv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-14T05:43:03Z","updated_at":"2020-01-14T05:43:29Z","body":"OK I still need to add more integration tests, but I am done hooking up plumbing, so this can be reviewed. @mattpap any suggestions for typescript improvements welcome.  I'd like to merge by Wednesday. Some new features:\r\n\r\n* calendar can be inline\r\n* calendar position can be given (non-inline)\r\n* enabled/disabled dates and date ranges can be provided\r\n\r\nFor later:\r\n\r\n* multiple date range selection\r\n\r\nHere is a test case to play with:\r\n```\r\nfrom bokeh.io import curdoc\r\nfrom bokeh.layouts import column\r\nfrom bokeh.models.widgets import DatePicker, Div, Button\r\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\r\n\r\ndp = DatePicker(title='Select start of sync date',\r\n    value=datetime(2019, 9, 20),\r\n    min_date=datetime(2019, 9, 1),\r\n    max_date=datetime.utcnow(),\r\n    # inline=True,\r\n    # position=\"above\",\r\n    # enabled_dates=[\"2019-09-12\", (\"2019-09-18\", datetime(2019, 9, 26))],\r\n    # enabled_dates=[\"2019-09-24\"],\r\n    css_classes=[\"foo\"])\r\n\r\ndef callback(attr,old,new):\r\n    print('old was {} and new is {}'.format(old,new))\r\n\r\ndp.on_change('value', callback)\r\n\r\nbutton = Button()\r\ndef cb(): dp.min_date = \"2019-09-15\"\r\nbutton.on_click(cb)\r\n\r\ncurdoc().add_root(column(button, *[Div(text=\"foo\") for _ in range(10)], dp, *[Div(text=\"foo\") for _ in range(10)], width=150))\r\n```\r\n\r\ncc @philippjfr still encourage to make sure `Date` property changes do not impact upstream. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/574012025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/574032846","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/pull/9509#issuecomment-574032846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/9509","id":574032846,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NDAzMjg0Ng==","user":{"login":"bryevdv","id":1078448,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg0NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1078448?v